@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home Page";
}

<!-- SECTION 1: Carousel Hero -->
<div id="bandCarousel" class="carousel slide position-relative shadow-lg" data-bs-ride="carousel">

    <div class="carousel-inner">
        <div class="carousel-item active">
            <img src="/images/BackPorch.jpg" class="d-block w-100" style="height: 700px; object-fit: cover; filter: brightness(40%);" alt="Band on the back porch">
        </div>
        <div class="carousel-item">
            <img src="/images/ChipLive.jpg" class="d-block w-100" style="height: 700px; object-fit: cover; filter: brightness(40%);" alt="Chip playing live">
        </div>
        <div class="carousel-item">
            <img src="/images/MichaelWendellLive.jpg" class="d-block w-100" style="height: 700px; object-fit: cover; filter: brightness(40%);" alt="Michael and Wendell live">
        </div>
        <div class="carousel-item">
            <img src="/images/RooftopPizzaSmoke.jpg" class="d-block w-100" style="height: 700px; object-fit: cover; filter: brightness(40%);" alt="Band hanging out on rooftop">
        </div>
        <div class="carousel-item">
            <img src="/images/WideShotLive.jpg" class="d-block w-100" style="height: 700px; object-fit: cover; filter: brightness(40%);" alt="Wide shot of live performance">
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Shortened Overlay for the Carousel -->
    <div class="position-absolute top-50 start-50 translate-middle text-center text-white" style="z-index: 10; width: 80%;">
        <h1 class="display-1 fw-bold mb-3">SHADYSIDE</h1>
        <p class="lead fw-normal mx-auto mb-4" style="max-width: 700px; font-size: 1.5rem;">
            The future is unwritten... but the band clearly has higher plans.
        </p>
        <div>
            <a href="/Merch" class="btn btn-success btn-lg fw-bold shadow-sm">
                <i class="bi bi-music-note-beamed me-2"></i> Get the New EP
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Navigation Controls -->
    <button class="carousel-control-prev" type="button" data-bs-target="#bandCarousel" data-bs-slide="prev">
        <span class="carousel-control-prev-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="visually-hidden">Previous</span>
    </button>
    <button class="carousel-control-next" type="button" data-bs-target="#bandCarousel" data-bs-slide="next">
        <span class="carousel-control-next-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="visually-hidden">Next</span>
    </button>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 2: Band Biography -->
<div class="container my-5 text-light">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-lg-8">
            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-4 border-bottom border-secondary pb-2">About Shadyside</h2>

            <p class="mb-3" style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.8;">
                What's that saying about loving something and setting it free, and it coming back later? Well, in mid '00s, Ohio's Shadyside set vocalist Michael Malarkey free to pursue studies at a prestigious London acting school. After two decades and a wildly successful stage and television career (Vampire Diaries, Law and Order: Organized Crime, Westworld, Project Bluebook, etc.), he returned.
            </p>

            <p class="mb-3" style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.8;">
                Formed in 1999, Shadyside cut a few demo tracks and some rough EPs while fleshing out their core lineup before adding Malarkey to the group in 2003. With their new vocalist secured, the band (rounded out by Vincent-Ryan Arceo on bass, Dave Brandenburg on drums, Adrian Grant on keys & guitar, Charles Heck on guitar & vocals, and Wendell Hensley on guitar & vocals) began to develop some momentum with a new EP that featured a more polishedThis is a fantastic, well-written bio that tells a great story about the band's history and reunion.

                From a web development and UI/UX (User Interface/User Experience) perspective, placing a massive three-paragraph block of text directly over a sliding image carousel will make it very difficult to read on smaller screens like mobile phones.

                ### Overview of the Solution

                To make your Home page look incredibly professional, we are going to split this content into two distinct sections:

                1.  **The Hook (Carousel Overlay):** We will extract a short, punchy, one-sentence summary from your text to serve as the hero text over the sliding images. This keeps the carousel clean and draws the user in.
                2.  **The Story (New Bio Section):** We will create a brand new HTML container right below the carousel dedicated to the full bio. I have slightly paraphrased the text you provided to optimize it for web readability, while ensuring the history—from the early Ohio days to locking in the groove on bass and drums, all the way to the Reel Love Recording sessions—remains completely intact.

                ### Implementation Instructions: Updating the Home Page

                1. Open **`Views/Home/Index.cshtml`**.
                2. Replace the entire file with this updated code. It includes your 5-image carousel from our last session, the new punchy overlay text, and the dedicated bio section below it.

